1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:10,180
This is the teacher. It explains, in plain words, and it has three modes: debrief, explain and course. You type the verb.

2
00:00:10,599 --> 00:00:22,706
Its file gives the three modes. Debrief is for the sentence Claude Code just wrote that did not land: it re-pitches that in plain words and says what follows, in under a minute.

3
00:00:22,706 --> 00:00:37,062
Explain is for a method or a paper: make the mechanism land, in one sitting. Course is a subject that takes weeks: the teacher recognises it, refuses it, and names the course skill.

4
00:00:37,449 --> 00:00:48,441
In debrief it has no network, ever, because a search query is outbound text and your session is not public. It never emits a link or a title it has not actually loaded.

5
00:00:48,441 --> 00:01:02,194
It states next steps; it does not interrogate you about them. And it does not draw what it could show: a real image first, then a video, and a drawing only when nothing suitable exists.

6
00:01:02,599 --> 00:01:12,012
A real run, in explain mode. A wet-lab biologist asks what a permutation test is and why the example uses five thousand of them.

7
00:01:12,012 --> 00:01:24,669
The verdict is Explained. Bullets, three technical terms each defined, the real numbers from the script it read, and a takeaway the reader can carry to the next problem.

8
00:01:25,049 --> 00:01:37,527
To use it, type the verb to Claude Code. Teacher debrief, at the sentence that lost you. Teacher explain, followed by the thing. Teacher course, followed by the subject.

9
00:01:37,527 --> 00:01:51,530
The first line is the verdict: Explained, or Gap. Gap is the teacher being honest that it cannot deliver, which is the point of it. Ask for a page only when you will annotate it.
